class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Key =
Status/Updates:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.2.4 was =
released<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.3.1 is in =
QA<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Patch merging to master is =
continuing and we now have a round of AUH upgrades to process. =
We&#8217;ve tried to merge some of the easier ones as there was =
autobuilder testing availability. This allows people to concentrate on =
the areas where there are issues with the automated upgrade and where we =
most need the help.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Anuj is unavailable for a few =
weeks so Richard will be acting as maintainer for hardknott until he =
returns (assistance welcome).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>An open letter about open =
source project work was sent to various mailing lists highlighting some =
of the challenges established project face from a resourcing =
perspective:<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
style=3D'mso-margin-top-alt:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin=
-left:.5in'><a =
href=3D"https://lists.openembedded.org/g/openembedded-architecture/topic/=
open_source_maintainers_an/82722442"><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:#1155CC'>https://lists.open=
embedded.org/g/openembedded-architecture/topic/open_source_maintainers_an=
/82722442</span></a><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The multiconfig changes in =
bitbake continue to cause problems, we still need simpler test cases to =
reproduce issues rather than huge builds. The existing patches seem to =
fix some workloads and break others. Richard is trying to fix but trying =
to fix autobuilder issues and other problems and these are slow builds =
to debug.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We saw a significant drop in =
open CVEs reported by the tooling against master this week (63 down to =
18) and hopefully many more of these have resolutions &#8220;in =
flight&#8221;. This will allow us to focus on the real issues and filter =
out the legacy noise.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>SMP was enabled for qemu on =
arm/x86 and we switched x86 to a more modern =
cpu/platform<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>One source of the OOM issues on =
the autobuilder appears to be glibc usermode testing going out of =
control and using up all system memory. We are investigating the best =
way to mitigate that but it accounts for some of our intermittent =
issues.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>When OOM issues occur an issue =
was identified in bitbake&#8217;s heartbeat events causing bitbake to =
hang. Ironically this was being heavily used by the recent autobuilder =
load debugging code. There is a patch pending to address =
this.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A rare sstate manifest =
corruption bug was tracked down thanks to information from Martin Jansa, =
a fix has been merged.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We have enabled more resource =
control on the autobuilder for xz memory/thread usage as that was =
contributing to the OOM issues. More investigation is needed into the =
rpm/deb controls for xz, help there would be =
appreciated.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l7 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent autobuilder issues =
continue to occur and are now at a record high level. You&nbsp; can see =
the list of failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the =
&#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
style=3D'mso-margin-top-alt:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin=
-left:.5in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>We are working to =
identify the load pattern on the infrastructure that seems to trigger =
these.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p =
style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
contribute:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are bugs identified as =
possible for newcomers to the project: <a =
href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Newcomers"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Newcomers</spa=
n></a><o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 level1 =
lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are bugs that are =
currently unassigned for YP 3.4. See: <a =
href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Bug_Triage#Medium.2B_3.4_Unass=
igned_Enhancements.2FBugs"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Bug_Triage#Med=
ium.2B_3.4_Unassigned_Enhancements.2FBugs</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></l=
i><li style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l5 =
level1 lfo10;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We&#8217;d welcome new =
maintainers for recipes in OE-Core. Please see the list at: <a =
href=3D"http://git.yoctoproject.org/cgit.cgi/poky/tree/meta/conf/distro/i=
nclude/maintainers.inc"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>http://git.yoctoproject.org/cgit.cgi/poky/tree/me=
ta/conf/distro/include/maintainers.inc</span></a> and discuss with the =
existing maintainer, or ask on the OE-Core mailing list. We will likely =
move a chunk of these to &#8220;Unassigned&#8221; soon to help =
facilitate this.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
